IELTS.lesson({"test": 5, "part": 3, "title": "Test 5, Part 3 — the discussion", "candidate": "hadi", "script": [{"who": "examiner", "text": "We've been talking about a journey that did not go as planned, and I'd like to discuss with you one or two more general questions related to this.", "ar": "كنّا نتحدّث عن رحلة لم تسر كما خُطّط لها، وأودّ أن أناقش معك سؤالاً أو سؤالين أعمّ يتعلّقان بهذا.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/b1019af47794155f.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Let's consider getting around a city.", "ar": "لنتناول التنقّل داخل المدينة.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/eab0554d987f6045.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "What are the main transport problems in big cities?", "ar": "ما أهمّ مشكلات المواصلات في المدن الكبيرة؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/4e60b95d63b74d97.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Traffic, mainly. There's too many cars for the roads in Hama, and the roads weren't built for this many cars, so you get traffic. And parking. Parking is a big problem also, because there's nowhere to put them.", "ar": "الازدحام، أساساً. هناك سيّارات أكثر مما تحتمل طرقات حماة، والطرقات لم تُبنَ لهذا العدد من السيّارات، فيحصل الازدحام. ومواقف السيّارات. المواقف مشكلة كبيرة أيضاً، لأنّه لا يوجد مكان نضعها فيه.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/795cdf1360e0b5db.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "How could cities encourage people to use public transport?", "ar": "كيف يمكن للمدن أن تشجّع الناس على استخدام النقل العام؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/02ea80feab932d2e.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Make it better, I suppose. If the buses are good and they come on time, people will use them. But if they're not good then people prefer their car, obviously, because it's more comfortable. The service taxis work because they come when you want them.", "ar": "أن تجعله أفضل، على ما أظنّ. إذا كانت الحافلات جيّدة وتأتي في موعدها فسيستخدمها الناس. أمّا إذا لم تكن جيّدة فيفضّل الناس سيّاراتهم، طبعاً، لأنّها أريح. السرافيس تنجح لأنّها تأتي حين تريدها.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/bacd0c8111d85417.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Should cars be banned from city centres?", "ar": "هل ينبغي منع السيّارات من مراكز المدن؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/4ae80883127c610e.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "That's difficult. In some cities maybe. In Hama the problem is that people need to… if you ban the cars, how do people get there? Unless the public transport is very good. So it comes back to the same thing really, it's the public transport.", "ar": "هذا صعب. في بعض المدن ربّما. في حماة المشكلة أنّ الناس يحتاجون الوصول إلى هناك، فإذا منعت السيّارات، كيف يصلون؟ إلّا إذا كان النقل العام جيّداً جداً. فالأمر يعود إلى الشيء نفسه في الحقيقة، إنّه النقل العام.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/e66ebf926de3cfe4.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Now let's talk about why people move.", "ar": "والآن لنتحدّث عن أسباب انتقال الناس.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/13e00b1789f8da8c.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Why do people move from the countryside to cities?", "ar": "لماذا ينتقل الناس من الريف إلى المدن؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/70f27afc3b6c8beb.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Work. That's most of it. Look, on my site about half the men are from villages an hour or two out, and they're not in Homs because they like Homs. They're there because the job is there. Some of them go back every weekend, four hours of travelling, every week.", "ar": "العمل. هذا معظم الأمر. انظر، في ورشتي نحو نصف الرجال من قرى تبعد ساعة أو ساعتين، وهم ليسوا في حمص لأنّهم يحبّون حمص. هم هناك لأنّ العمل هناك. بعضهم يعود كلّ نهاية أسبوع، أربع ساعات سفر، كلّ أسبوع.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/3e9d4ad63b397fe0.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "What problems does this movement cause?", "ar": "ما المشكلات التي يسبّبها هذا الانتقال؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/5f4097e8c70e4c0b.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "For the cities, it's pressure. More people in the same houses, so the prices go up because nobody is building. And for the villages around Hama it's the opposite, the young people leave and the village becomes old people only. Both are a problem but in a different way.", "ar": "بالنسبة للمدن، هو ضغط. ناس أكثر في البيوت نفسها، فترتفع الأسعار لأنّ لا أحد يبني. وبالنسبة للقرى حول حماة العكس، الشباب يغادرون وتصبح القرية كبار سنّ فقط. الاثنان مشكلة لكن بطريقة مختلفة.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/613ca9a11b7e567d.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you think governments should try to stop this movement?", "ar": "هل تظنّ أنّ على الحكومات أن تحاول إيقاف هذا الانتقال؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/548b7ec091086cff.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Hmm. I don't think you can stop it, really. You could maybe, if there was work in the villages near Hama then people would stay, so maybe that. But I don't know how you do that. Yeah, I don't really know.", "ar": "همم. لا أظنّ أنّه يمكن إيقافه، في الحقيقة. يمكن ربّما، لو كان هناك عمل في القرى قرب حماة لبقي الناس، فربّما ذلك. لكنّني لا أعرف كيف يُفعل ذلك. نعم، لا أعرف حقّاً.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/a88eeee5d0ab18c6.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Thank you. That is the end of the speaking test.", "ar": "شكراً لك. بهذا ينتهي اختبار المحادثة.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/f502144bdfbbc476.mp3"}], "boxes": [{"q": "What are the main transport problems in big cities?", "topic": "Getting around a city", "model": "Traffic, mainly. There's too many cars for the roads in Hama, and the roads weren't built for this many cars, so you get traffic. And parking. Parking is a big problem also, because there's nowhere to put them.", "modelBand": 6.5, "why": "(attempted CONTRAST)"}, {"q": "How could cities encourage people to use public transport?", "topic": "Getting around a city", "model": "Make it better, I suppose. If the buses are good and they come on time, people will use them. But if they're not good then people prefer their car, obviously, because it's more comfortable. The service taxis work because they come when you want them.", "modelBand": 6.5, "why": "(attempted SPECULATE)"}, {"q": "Should cars be banned from city centres?", "topic": "Getting around a city", "model": "That's difficult. In some cities maybe. In Hama the problem is that people need to… if you ban the cars, how do people get there? Unless the public transport is very good. So it comes back to the same thing really, it's the public transport.", "modelBand": 6.5, "why": "(attempted QUALIFY)"}, {"q": "Why do people move from the countryside to cities?", "topic": "Why people move", "model": "Work. That's most of it. Look, on my site about half the men are from villages an hour or two out, and they're not in Homs because they like Homs. They're there because the job is there. Some of them go back every weekend, four hours of travelling, every week.", "modelBand": 6.5, "why": "(partial recovery — EXEMPLIFY)"}, {"q": "What problems does this movement cause?", "topic": "Why people move", "model": "For the cities, it's pressure. More people in the same houses, so the prices go up because nobody is building. And for the villages around Hama it's the opposite, the young people leave and the village becomes old people only. Both are a problem but in a different way.", "modelBand": 6.5, "why": "(attempted CONCEDE)"}, {"q": "Do you think governments should try to stop this movement?", "topic": "Why people move", "model": "Hmm. I don't think you can stop it, really. You could maybe, if there was work in the villages near Hama then people would stay, so maybe that. But I don't know how you do that. Yeah, I don't really know.", "modelBand": 6.5, "why": "(abandoned)"}], "voices": {"examiner": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "candidate": "piper-en_US-ryan-medium-s120"}});
